    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23818" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insessor</span></b> , ōris, m.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				besetter</i>, <i>occupant</i> (very rare); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">of a ship,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Jul. Val. Res Gest. Alex. 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">viarum,</span>”
				<i>a waylayer</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 2, 48</span></i>
			; cf.: insessores, latrones, Paul. ex <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				111</span></i> Müll.: quod circa vias insidientur sedentes.
				</div>
